course: dictionary
lesson: 7651
title: Promise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A promise is your word that you will certainly do something, so other people can count on you. «I promise I will be home by six.» Promise can also be a noun: you make a promise, or you keep a promise.
explain: Keeping a promise builds trust. Breaking one hurts people, so do not promise what you cannot do. «I'll think about it» is not a promise, because it does not say you will do anything at all.
explain: Some promises do not count. If someone asks you to promise a secret that makes you feel unsafe, you do not have to keep it. Tell a trusted adult straight away.
explain: Promise has a second meaning: to show signs that something will happen or be good. «Dark clouds promise rain» means rain is likely to come, and «a promising young player» is someone who may become very good.
fact: A promise is a word you give that you will certainly do something.
fact: As a verb, promise changes: I promise, she promised, they are promising.
fact: «Dark clouds promise rain» means the clouds show signs that rain is coming.
fact: «A promise to hide wrongdoing does not bind you.» A bad promise does not make a wrong thing right.
fact: A promise forced by a threat, or one that controls who you can be friends with, does not count.
exercise: «Coming in when the street lights come on is a promise to the people waiting for you.» What is this promise? | To hide in the park | To buy a new bike | To ignore the street lights | *To come home at the right time
exercise: «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat from a site that promised free gems.» What does promised mean here? | Broke her computer | Hid the gems from her friends | *Said it would certainly give her free gems | Asked her mum for money
exercise: What does «a promising young player» mean? | A player who is very old | Someone who never plays | *Someone who may become very good | Someone who has broken every rule
test: What should you do if a stranger asks you to promise to keep a secret that makes you feel unsafe? | Keep the promise and say nothing | *Tell a trusted adult straight away | Make the promise and tell a friend | Wait and see what happens
test: Which word is a noun in «She made a promise to call me»? | *promise | she | made | call
exam: Which is the best meaning of promise in «Dark clouds promise rain»? | *To show signs that something will happen | To hide from the rain | To break something | To say you will certainly do something
